---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { projectFamily, recordedDay } from '../lib/project-family.mjs';
import { reviewLabel } from '../lib/date-label.mjs';
import { ArrowRight } from '@lucide/astro';

const family = projectFamily();
const asOf = reviewLabel(family.asOf) ?? family.asOf;
const groups = [...family.groups].sort((left, right) =>
  Number(right.id === 'showcased') - Number(left.id === 'showcased'));
const day = (value: string | null | undefined) => {
  const date = recordedDay(value);
  return date ? reviewLabel(date) ?? date : null;
};
---
<Base title="Project family" description="Explore Media Studio and the apps you can build with App Composer, then browse the wider portfolio of working software.">
 <header class="family-intro">
  <div class="family-copy">
   <p class="eyebrow">App Composer projects</p>
   <h1>See what you can build.</h1>
   <p class="lede">Give your agent a brief and keep the app it builds. Start from a working example, then make your own version with its own source, data and release.</p>
   <div class="family-actions">
    <a class="button" href="/ready">Get ready to build <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true"/></a>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/blueprints">Explore blueprints</a>
   </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="flagship-image">
   <a href="/media-studio"><img src="/media-studio/studio-library-20261114.jpg" width="1600" height="1000" alt="Open the Media Studio build story" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"/></a>
   <figcaption>The working Media Studio library, with saved takes and an assembled cut.</figcaption>
  </figure>
 </header>

 <section class="family-feature" aria-labelledby="flagship">
  <div>
   <p class="eyebrow">Composer reference app</p>
   <h2 id="flagship">Media Studio</h2>
  </div>
  <div>
   <p>Create images and clips, cut a short film and publish it from a studio you can run yourself. See the Composer build, download a brief for your own Studio, or try the browser-local image tools right now.</p>
   <div class="family-actions">
    <a href="/media-studio">Read the build story <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true"/></a>
    <a href="https://media.loftwah.com/tools/images">Try Image Tools <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true"/></a>
    <a href="/media-studio/studio">Open your Studio <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true"/></a>
   </div>
   <details class="flagship-receipt" open={Astro.url.searchParams.get("example") === "creative-handoff"}>
    <summary>Media Studio build and release record</summary>
    <ol>
     <li><strong>First release.</strong> Studio went live on 13 November 2026 from <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/commit/c6ee157451a5f28f3ae36e58e2bb17be3ef63fa3">Studio source c6ee157</a>, the <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/blob/afce1a5a96651db7088b63fb0a1c59ede7d6a4da/config/media-studio-standalone.json">revision Composer Init pinned for that release</a>. <a href="https://media.loftwah.com/build.json">Check the current live build</a>.</li>
     <li><strong>Resume an existing Studio project.</strong> After <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/pull/314">Studio #314</a> shipped, an unreadable input left the same contact-sheet PNG, layout JSON and ZIP downloadable. The existing owner then returned through Composer to the same saved After Hours storyboard, revision 5. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/issues/600#issuecomment-6961935820">Read the production checks</a>.</li>
     <li><strong>Build a listening timer from owned artwork.</strong> The owner exported a palette from Fighter’s Gutter Grin artwork in Studio, applied a swatch in Launch Kit and adopted the icons and social image in Composer Init. The Composer CLI built the timer from the adopted files. All 13 generated file hashes matched, and the timer started, paused and reset in a local browser. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/issues/600#issuecomment-6962720182">Read the local build and playback checks</a>.</li>
     <li>
      <strong>Try a palette handoff.</strong> Open <a href="https://media.loftwah.com/tools/images">Image Tools</a>, load the sample, extract its palette and download the JSON.
      Choose <strong>Use palette in Launch Kit</strong>, select your JSON and apply a swatch. <strong>Continue into Composer</strong> downloads the ZIP and opens <a href="/init/launch-kit">the review</a>, where you select that ZIP.
      In a 390px-wide Chrome window, the ZIP carried the applied colour <code>#80cba1</code> and Composer displayed two rendered previews. We stopped at the import review. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/issues/600#issuecomment-6945773550">Read the verified workflow</a>.
     </li>
     <li><strong>Replay brief.</strong> The <a href="/media-studio/media-studio-brief-20261114.json" download>Paper &amp; Light specification</a> was exported from Composer Init on 14 November. It starts a replay from <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/commit/fec91ba3e25e8349f8d891a22f676980686fce76">Studio source fec91ba</a>, a later revision. <a href="/blueprints#media-studio">Open the Media Studio blueprint</a> for its preset, locked apps and the evidence behind it.</li>
     <li><strong>Palette export.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/pull/186">Studio #186</a> added CSS palette export. We used <a href="https://woodhouse.loftwah.com/campaign/20261113-build-notes/foilbury-foil-bench-preview.jpg">Foilbury artwork from Woodhouse Share</a> and verified that the CSS and GIMP downloads contained the same eight colours.</li>
     <li><strong>Artwork search.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/pull/189">Studio #189</a> added Woodhouse artwork search to the same Studio. In the Foilbury project, we selected “A finish catches light · Build note” by title and checked its credit and original link before import. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/issues/64#issuecomment-6935179738">Selection evidence</a> · <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/commit/c1ed37ac4bdcdda64cc8037646cc03475d64f5e5">Studio source c1ed37ac</a>.</li>
     <li id="creative-handoff"><strong>From artwork to an app draft.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/pull/193">Studio #193</a> exported eight colours from the <a href="https://woodhouse.loftwah.com/campaign/20261113-build-notes/foilbury-foil-bench-preview.jpg">Foilbury build-note artwork by Woodhouse</a>. We applied one swatch in <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer-launch-kit/pull/17">Launch Kit #17</a> and downloaded this card. <a href="/init/launch-kit">Composer Init</a> reviewed the package and adopted it into a separate app draft on this device.
      <figure class="receipt-sample">
       <a href="/launch-kit/cards/foilbury-launch-palette-social-20261117.png"><img src="/launch-kit/cards/foilbury-launch-palette-social-20261117.png" width="1200" height="630" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Foilbury card with a gold-foil paper tag on an illustrated workbench, framed in plum"/></a>
       <figcaption>Open the 1200 × 630 card generated by Launch Kit.</figcaption>
      </figure>
     </li>
     <li><strong>Web-ready images.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/pull/195">Studio #195</a> added a local WebP preset. At desktop and phone widths, the <a href="https://woodhouse.loftwah.com/campaign/20261113-share-studio/foilbury-sticker-moss-preview.png">Foilbury Moss artwork from Woodhouse</a> stayed 1200 × 1200 and went from 1,365,546 to 153,240 bytes. The export kept 563,105 fully transparent pixels and the original file was preserved. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/issues/183#issuecomment-6937217543">Web-ready images release record</a>.</li>
     <li><strong>Image export receipt.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/pull/196">Studio #196</a> added a JSON receipt with the exact source and output hashes, dimensions and settings. The same Moss PNG produced the same 153,240-byte WebP on desktop and phone. The downloaded receipt stayed identical when the rotation control changed after export. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/issues/183#issuecomment-6937400509">Image export receipt record</a>.</li>
     <li><strong>Social kit export.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/pull/204">Studio #204</a> added four social sizes and a downloadable ZIP with a receipt for each image. Download the <a href="https://woodhouse.loftwah.com/campaign/20261113-share-studio/foilbury-sticker-moss-preview.png">Foilbury Moss PNG from Woodhouse</a>, select it in <a href="https://media.loftwah.com/tools/images">Image Tools</a> and choose <strong>Make 4 social sizes</strong>. Our signed-out desktop and phone runs kept the transparent pixels and produced matching WebPs at 1080 × 1080, 1080 × 1350, 1080 × 1920 and 1920 × 1080. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio/issues/183#issuecomment-6938735525">Social kit release record</a>.</li>
     <li><strong>Check the public guide before sharing.</strong> Open <a href="https://share.loftwah.com/">Link Check</a> and paste the URL of <a href="/media-studio/direct">Make the next shot count</a>. On 17 November, our run found the exact canonical URL and 23 passing checks, with four items to review. <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/issues/625#issuecomment-6942651327">Read the live inspection record</a>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>These releases were built and verified by the Studio operator. An independent owner replay is still pending. <a href="/creator-hub#follow-up">See the Creator Hub build and its follow-up</a>.</p>
   </details>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="family-feature" aria-labelledby="prints-desktop-project">
  <div>
   <h2 id="prints-desktop-project">Prints Desktop</h2>
  </div>
  <div>
   <p>Explore Afterlight, six speculative landscapes in an independent Rust and Rune creative workspace. Open the Mac preview and keep any of the included original images.</p>
   <div class="family-actions">
    <a href="/prints-desktop">See Prints Desktop <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true"/></a>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 {groups.filter(group => group.projects.length > 0).map(group => (
  <section class="tier-group" id={`tier-${group.id}`} aria-labelledby={`tier-${group.id}-heading`}>
   <header class="tier-heading">
    <h2 id={`tier-${group.id}-heading`}>{group.id === 'showcased' ? 'From the portfolio' : group.label}</h2>
    {group.id === 'showcased' && <p>Explore working software from our wider portfolio. Project and release details were recorded on {asOf}.</p>}
   </header>
   <ul class="project-list">
    {group.projects.map(project => (
     <li class="project-card" data-project={project.id} data-tier={project.tier}>
      <h3>{project.name}</h3>
      <p>{project.summary}</p>
      <div class="project-links">
       {project.canonicalUrl ? (
        <a href={project.canonicalUrl}>Open {project.name} <ArrowRight size={15} aria-hidden="true"/></a>
       ) : (
        <span class="not-recorded">Live address not recorded</span>
       )}
       <a href={project.dossier}>Project record</a>
      </div>
      <details class="project-details">
       <summary>Project and release details</summary>
       <dl>
        <dt>Relationship to Composer</dt>
        <dd>{group.label}. {project.evidence}</dd>
        <dt>Recorded status</dt>
        <dd>
         {project.discipline} · {project.lifecycle} · {project.state}
         {project.live && <span>HTTP {project.live.status} on {day(project.live.observedAt)} · {project.live.title}</span>}
         {project.probe && <span>HTTP {project.probe.status} on {day(project.probe.observedAt)} · {project.probe.reason}</span>}
        </dd>
        <dt>Source revision</dt>
        <dd>
         {project.sourcePin ? (
          <><code>{project.sourcePin}</code>{day(project.sourceObservedAt) && <span>Observed {day(project.sourceObservedAt)}</span>}</>
         ) : (
          <span class="not-recorded">not recorded</span>
         )}
         {project.sourceNote && <span>{project.sourceNote}</span>}
        </dd>
        <dt>Blueprint</dt>
        <dd>{project.blueprint ? (
         <a href={`/blueprints#${project.blueprint.id}`}>{project.blueprint.id}</a>
        ) : (
         <span class="not-recorded">blueprint not recorded</span>
        )}</dd>
       </dl>
      </details>
     </li>
    ))}
   </ul>
  </section>
 ))}

 <details class="family-method" id="provenance">
  <summary>How we record project provenance</summary>
  <p>Each relationship reflects evidence collected by {asOf}. The live status comes from that dated record.</p>
  <dl>
   {family.groups.map(group => (
    <div><dt>{group.label}</dt><dd>{group.meaning}</dd></div>
   ))}
  </dl>
 </details>
</Base>
<style>
 .family-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.92fr) minmax(0,1.08fr);gap:clamp(24px,5vw,72px);align-items:center;padding-block:32px 44px}
 .family-copy h1{font-size:clamp(2.65rem,5.5vw,5rem);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.04em;max-width:12ch;margin:12px 0 20px}
 .family-copy .lede{max-width:49ch}
 .family-actions,.project-links{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px 20px;flex-wrap:wrap}
 .family-actions{margin-top:22px}
 .family-actions a,.project-links a{display:inline-flex;gap:7px;align-items:center;min-height:44px}
 .flagship-image{margin:0}
 .flagship-image img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px}
 .flagship-image figcaption{font-size:.86rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:10px}
 .family-feature{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;gap:18px 36px;padding-block:28px 36px;border-block:1px solid var(--color-border)}
 .family-feature h2,.tier-heading h2{margin:0;font-size:clamp(1.75rem,3.2vw,2.55rem)}
 .family-feature .eyebrow{margin:0 0 8px}
 .family-feature p{max-width:65ch}
 .family-feature div:nth-child(2)>p,.family-feature .family-actions{margin:0}
 .flagship-receipt{margin-top:18px;max-width:65ch;color:var(--color-muted)}
 .flagship-receipt summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--color-foreground)}
 .flagship-receipt ol{padding-inline-start:1.4rem}
 .flagship-receipt li + li{margin-top:8px}
 .flagship-receipt .receipt-sample{margin:12px 0 0}
 .flagship-receipt .receipt-sample a{display:block;width:100%}
 .flagship-receipt .receipt-sample img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px}
 .flagship-receipt .receipt-sample figcaption{font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.5;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:8px}
 .tier-group{padding-block:42px 15px}
 .tier-heading p{max-width:65ch;color:var(--color-muted)}
 .project-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;list-style:none;margin:22px 0 0;padding:0;max-width:none}
 .project-card{min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px}
 .project-card h3{font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 10px}
 .project-card p{color:var(--color-muted);margin:0 0 10px}
 .project-links{margin-top:auto;font-size:.92rem}
 .project-details{border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);margin-top:7px}
 .project-details summary,.family-method summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;padding-block:12px;font-weight:600}
 .project-details dl{font-size:.9rem;margin:0}
 .project-details dt,.family-method dt{font-weight:650;margin-top:12px}
 .project-details dd,.family-method dd{margin:4px 0;color:var(--color-muted);overflow-wrap:anywhere}
 .project-details dd span{display:block}
 .not-recorded{color:var(--color-muted)}
 .family-method{border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);margin-top:32px;padding-block:12px 24px;max-width:78ch}
 @media(max-width:930px){.project-list{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.family-intro{gap:24px}}
 @media(max-width:660px){.family-intro,.family-feature,.project-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}.family-intro{padding-block:16px 30px}.project-card{padding:16px}.tier-group{padding-block:28px 10px}}
</style>
